## Summary

The bug: when a section directory existed in multiple languages but had no `_index.md`, only the language whose page was processed first got its section page synthesized. Other languages with content under that section were missing their section page.

The fix in `hugolib/content_map_page_assembler.go`:

1. Extracted the existing missing-vectors handler (event listener + post-walk hook) into a `setupMissingHomeOrRootSectionHandler` closure so it can be reused.
2. After synthesizing a missing root section in `transformPagesAndCreateMissingHome`, install the same handler so that pages from other languages walked later will register those languages as missing — and the post-walk hook then creates section pages for them.
3. Added a `fromContentOnly` flag: for synthesized sections it ignores `KindTaxonomy`/`KindTerm` events so an empty-language taxonomy under the section doesn't trigger creation of an empty section page in that language (preserves `TestTaxonomyNestedEmptySectionsIssue12188`).
